# Editing AGENTS.md

AGENTS.md loads into every agent session, so each line costs context every time. Keep it to rules an agent needs in most sessions. Mechanics, history, and detail go in `notes/`, with a one-line pointer from AGENTS.md.

## Before adding a line

- Is it needed in most sessions? If not, write a note in `notes/`, add it to `notes/00_overview.md`, and point to it.
- Does a note already say it? Link to the note. Do not repeat it.
- Is it how something works? Put the explanation in a note. AGENTS.md keeps the hard rule.
- Describe the current state only. Do not record what changed or what used to be true.

## Before removing a line

- Do not delete a rule just to shorten the file. Move the detail to a note, and keep the hard rule and the pointer in AGENTS.md.
- Check that the moved text is in the note before deleting it from AGENTS.md.

## Size

There is no hard size limit. When AGENTS.md grows noticeably, review it against `local/agent-lookup-log.md`. A fact agents keep searching for belongs near the top. A long rule that is rarely needed belongs in a note. Ask the user before cutting a rule.
